  "known_limitations": [
    "KEV positive class is small -- model may miss novel exploit patterns",
    "attack_vector/complexity/privileges_required/user_interaction/scope were NOT available in this NVD source and default to -1 (unknown) -- SHAP confirms these contribute zero signal",
    "EPSS/NVD are global feeds -- India-specific signal only from CERT-In curated list",
    "Temporal AUC lower than random-split AUC -- expected and disclosed",
    "At the binary reference threshold (0.975), recall is 48.1% -- roughly half of confirmed-exploited CVEs fall below the strict cutoff. False-negative analysis shows two distinct patterns: (a) borderline cases scoring 0.94-0.96, just under threshold, recoverable by using a lower operating tier; and (b) a genuine blind spot of ~34 high-CVSS/high-EPSS CVEs (EPSS > 0.5) that the model underrates even so -- e.g. CVSS 9.3-9.8 with EPSS 0.82-0.87 scored as low as 0.19-0.46 probability. CRISPR mitigates this by using probability_bands and recall_at_k ranking rather than a single binary cutoff for remediation prioritization: at K=500 the model surfaces 60.7% of all confirmed exploits, and at K=1000, 73.3%, which is the operative metric for a limited-capacity security team rather than the binary precision/recall pair alone."
  ],
